    "id": "distribute",
    "language": "Okay, so in this one scenario, when, when you look around, you see your right winger is marked, your left winger is also marked. Your left striker is between two men over there, and your s- right striker would be your best option. So what you should do is if you're[0] passing, you should pass to your right striker, uh, with this button. [1]After[2] you make the pass, your right striker now has the ball. The defender... And it's facing, the back of your right striker is facing the defender, so if he turns, the defender will most likely take his ball. So what you should do after you pass, you should provide a supporting run, and you should run from here, that this will provide an option for the right striker, and he can one-two with your right striker. Your right striker can pass it to you here, and you can just score.",
